domain VT109:
  description "Implement the accepted fixed V3 candidate review-to-activation path on existing cc304."
problem P1:
  |
    vt101 only directly imported SQLite fixtures. Ordinary persisted attempt,
    preview and confirm paths parse V2 envelopes. The accepted R18 review and
    atomic activation obligation remains in vt109, now runnable in canonical PERT.
evidence E1:
  |
    Source 11a89da has V2-only candidate types, save validation, preview projection
    and append schemaVersion in character-assets-v2.ts/routes.ts. Existing
    CharacterReviewPage can render structured V3 review fields. Existing current
    generation selection already reads V3 readiness. Fixed importer bypasses review.
evidence E2:
  |
    Owner now says proceed in order. Accepted V3 authoring v5 SHA256
    17596f17d6514d5ada160b9d95453ab2bcb9cee9e4b2d2991acb8238b55ee27b
    R18 and ADR0010/0014 require persisted exact owner-reviewed candidates,
    no provider in confirmation and atomic append/CAS. Child PERT selects vt109.
premise OPTIONS:
  |
    A new import-only activation API repeats the bypass. Reuse existing attempts,
    owner review route/UI and transaction, with a properly parsed V2/V3 envelope
    union and V3 content/digest confirmation. Keep V2 battle readers unchanged;
    explicit V3 ready read serves registration until vt102 governs Battle consumers.
premise UNKNOWNS:
  |
    Inspect PostgreSQL harness availability and worker job closing before choosing
    exact tests. Paid provider generation, Stage data and new Battle architecture
    remain separate tasks. Existing focused generated-V3 general mode completion
    remains downstream; this task delivers the fixed-candidate registration path.
decision D1 based_on P1, E1, E2, OPTIONS, UNKNOWNS:
  |
    Start vt109 with actual timestamp. Validate and project persisted candidates
    in one narrow pure module. Extend ordinary save/review/activate to V3,
    binding exact reviewed digest, guarding stale/terminal/CAS paths and preserving
    V2 tests. Prepare fixed Neva/Rio candidates atomically as review-waiting attempts
    with finished generation jobs; command prepares, owner UI confirms. Provide
    complete structured owner review and digest in existing review DTO/UI without
    frontend refactor. Use shared transaction abstraction on SQLite/Postgres.
    Test prepare/review/confirm/select and retries/conflicts/rollback/unauthorized
    actions through real routes and DBs; record limitations honestly. Verify before
    completion, then update canonical remaining estimates from measured actuals.
evidence E3:
  |
    The independent review identified missing source comparison and fixture-local
    attempt provenance. The revised implementation persists the original source,
    verifies its digest, binds provenance to the actual attempt, and displays source
    and added details. The reviewer closed both INSIDE findings. Diagnostic SQLite
    tests cover real owner routes, digest rejection, duplicate replay, decline,
    expiry and rollback. PostgreSQL server binaries and a configured test target
    are absent; PostgreSQL runtime behavior remains unobserved.
premise TEST_AUTHORITY:
  |
    ADR0034 requires exact source-bound verification Seals and current Causes.
    Direct test success alone is diagnostic. Review the final implementation and
    source manifest, link the verification to Accepted R18 and ADR0010/0014 plus
    ADR0034, then run the selected tests. This records conformance evidence and
    does not accept a new requirement or architecture.
decision D2 based_on D1, E3, TEST_AUTHORITY:
  |
    Publish a bounded local implementation manifest and verification basis for
    vt109, leaving old verification generations historical. Run the canonical
    test selector and exact UI tests, then finish vt109 only after passing checks.
    Record measured actual duration and let perttool observe velocity for vt109
    alone; exclude vt101 partial timing from throughput. Use tool-produced
    remaining-path estimates and disclose the single-task sample and absent PG
    runtime evidence. Keep new Battle implementation pending the cc319 decision.
